  "description": "The existing synchronous Quilt social-network call graph with illustrative payload and backend-traffic budgets.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Every edge is invoked once per successful workflow execution; N=100 is a synthetic profiling window.",
    "CPU values are illustrative average active core equivalents; memory is illustrative peak host MiB per invocation, including runtime overhead. Neither was measured.",
    "Local storage and external network values are bytes per function invocation. Edge request/response values are body-size budgets per call; they are excluded from node external-network totals.",
    "External object stores, caches, and databases are not mergeable function nodes. Merging does not automatically remove their traffic.",
    "Connection setup, retries, transport overhead, client-to-entry traffic, and execution timing are not modeled. No bandwidth rate or latency prediction is implied.",
    "Zero means no modeled demand for this selected workload, not an observed production measurement.",
    "Successful post: one URL, two mentioned users, two media identifiers, and twenty followers. Mentioned users are disjoint from followers, yielding twenty-two home-timeline updates.",
    "Both lookup caches miss for this request: user mentions and follower lookup query memcached then Redis. Runtimes are warm; this is a chosen request profile, not a measured cache-hit distribution.",
    "The supplied synchronous Rust implementation makes blocking calls in program order. Graph siblings are not necessarily parallel; edges represent actual calls, not a stage-by-stage dataflow diagram.",
    "media-service validates and repackages identifiers/types; compose-creator-with-userid formats an existing ID and username. Neither fetches media objects or queries a database.",
    "The checked-in storage implementation uses Redis, not the MongoDB deployment of upstream DeathStarBench.",
    "Remote network budgets are illustrative protocol/body allowances. Eight post-field HSETs are budgeted at 2304 bytes sent and 64 bytes received; URL shortening uses two HSETs at 128/8 bytes each.",
    "Each timeline ZADD is budgeted at 96 sent bytes and 8 reply bytes. Lookup budgets include cache-miss and Redis traffic; source code has no additional function calls for these backend operations.",
    "Post and text call payload budgets are 2048 bytes. The graph does not include retries, failures, or input validation exits."
  ],
